logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# No trailing slash: `node_modules/` matches a directory only, so a SYMLINK by
# that name — which is how a worktree under .claude/worktrees resolves its
# `link:` siblings without a second install — read as an untracked file and
# landed in an `add -A`.
node_modules
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm
.eslintcache
*.tgz
.env
.env.test
meta.json
test-screenshots/
.test-jbrowse-*/
.vscode
# Claude Code's scratch, including the git worktrees it checks out under
# .claude/worktrees. Untracked but not ignored, it left the tree permanently
# unclean, and `pnpm version` refuses to run on one — so a release could be
# blocked by an unrelated session's working directory.
.claude/
.wasm-build/
# OGDF's own build tree, inside the vendored sources. ~85 MB of objects and one
# libOGDF.a; the sources beside it ARE committed (see vendor/README.md).
vendor/ogdf/build-wasm/
# The host-arch pair of the two above, built by scripts/profile/build.sh so perf
# has symbols to walk. Deliberately a separate tree: dropping a native libOGDF.a
# on build-wasm/ would silently relink the committed engine against it.
.profile-build/
vendor/ogdf/build-native/
